BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://houstonarboretum.o
 rg/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Green-Tree-Frog-on-leaf.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://houstonarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2
 026/04/Green-Tree-Frog-on-leaf.jpg
UID:z3fV7Z5aGQUWe_DCzXm2u
SUMMARY:Froggy Night
DTSTAMP:20260814T042943Z
DTSTART:20260815T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:$37 member / $52 nonmemberInstructor: Dr. Cassidy Johnson Ages 
	21+ \n\n\n\nHop on over for a wet\, wild night! Enjoy refreshments (frog-t
	hemed snacks\, coffee\, and Saint Arnold Brewing Company beer) while you l
	earn all about the strange and wonderful world of frogs\, from their croak
	ing courtship to their mysterious metamorphosis. Weather permitting\, we’l
	l also go for a hike to search for frogs and other nocturnal creatures. \n
	\n\n\nPlease dress for the weather and wear walking shoes. \n\n\n\n\nsold 
	out\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nInstructor bio: Dr. Cassidy Johnson has a B.S. and M.
	S. in Biology at Texas A&M University – Corpus Christi and a Ph.D. in Bioc
	hemistry & Cell Biology from Rice University. She loves teaching biology a
	nd is currently an Assistant Teaching Professor for Rice BioSciences. She 
	fell in love with local amphibians while working for the Houston toad ex s
	itu conservation program at the Houston Zoo. She is also passionate about 
	the protection and restoration of Texas prairies and is on the board of th
	e Native Prairie Association of Texas and was previously the president of 
	the Coastal Prairie Partnership.\n\nhttps://houstonarboretum.org/event/fro
	ggy-night/\n\nFrom Houston Arboretum & Nature Center
URL:https://houstonarboretum.org/event/froggy-night/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:houston-arboretum
CATEGORIES:Houston Arboretum & Nature Center
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
